  "dimensions": [
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_e7a31c7f",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image shows a black corrugated pipe on a beach with the text 'no wonder why the pipes are not working.' The visual juxtaposition of the pipe with the ocean and beach setting implies a humorous or sarcastic commentary on infrastructure failure, likely suggesting the pipes are ineffective because they are exposed to the elements or are improperly placed. There is no direct or indirect attack on any protected group, nor is there abusive, cyberbullying, misogynistic, or propagandistic content. The meme's intent is to use absurd or ironic imagery to comment on a mundane problem (non-functioning pipes) in a lighthearted or sarcastic way, which may be perceived as harmless humor by some but could be interpreted as dismissive or unhelpful by others. The overall intent is not harmful in a direct or targeted way, but the humor may trivialize a real infrastructure issue, which could be seen as potentially harmful in context.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_f9353104"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
